## 4) Priority-1: Max Execution Duration Guard (mandatory)

Add a guard check **before every step**:

```apex
public with sharing class ExecutionGuards {
    public static void assertNotTimedOut(Orch_Execution__c execRec) {
        if (execRec.StartedAt__c == null) return;
        Integer maxSec = (execRec.MaxDurationSeconds__c == null || execRec.MaxDurationSeconds__c <= 0)
            ? 3600 // default 1h; change per enterprise policy
            : Integer.valueOf(execRec.MaxDurationSeconds__c);

        Long elapsedMs = System.now().getTime() - execRec.StartedAt__c.getTime();
        if (elapsedMs > (Long)maxSec * 1000L) {
            // hard stop
            execRec.Status__c = 'TimedOut';
            execRec.EndedAt__c = System.now();
            update execRec;
            throw new AuraHandledException('Execution timed out (max duration exceeded).');
        }
    }
}
